04-Jun-2026 (05:13:18 PM) - INFO - Arguments: {"emails":[{"id":"19e925de4d57fbd2","subject":"Re: Job Opportunity at Barclays | BA4 - Data Scientist","body":"Subject: Re: Job Opportunity at Barclays | BA4 - Data Scientist\n\nHi Megha,\n\nThank you for reaching out regarding the opportunity at Barclays. I appreciate the details shared.\n\nPlease find the requested information below:\n- Current CTC: 12 LPA\n- Expected CTC: 24 LPA\n- Notice Period: 3 months\n- Reason For Change: I am looking for opportunities that offer greater responsibilities and align more closely with my expertise in data science and AI.\n\nIn response to your questions:\n- Yes, I have hands-on experience with PySpark in data processing and analysis projects.\n- I have experience working with unstructured data, particularly in developing AI models that process textual data.\n- I have approximately 2 years of experience in Data Science and Analytics, mostly focused on AI and machine learning models.\n\nPlease let me know if there is anything else you require from my side. I am looking forward to discussing this opportunity further.\n\nBest regards,\nManu Yadav\n\nContact: +91-7791997383\nEmail: peyadavmanu57@gmail.com\nLinkedIn: /in/manuyadav"},{"id":"19e925de46920f68","subject":"Re: Job Opportunity at KPMG | Con\\AM - Generative AI Engineer","body":"Subject: Re: Job Opportunity at KPMG | Con\\AM - Generative AI Engineer\n\nHi Riya,\n\nThank you for considering my application for the Generative AI Engineer position at KPMG. I am keen to pursue this opportunity and have provided the requested details below:\n\n- Current CTC: 12 LPA\n- Expected CTC: 24 LPA\n- Notice Period: 3 months\n- Reason For Job Change: I am looking to leverage my skills in an organization that emphasizes innovation in AI technologies.\n\nRegarding your questions:\n- Yes, I have experience developing AI models using TensorFlow and PyTorch, assisting in various projects focused on generative AI solutions.\n- I have implemented advanced AI techniques, including using reinforcement learning in several projects, aimed at optimizing model performance.\n- I have experience deploying AI models in cloud environments, particularly using Google Cloud Platform and have familiarity with Azure practices.\n- Yes, I have engaged in projects utilizing the Retrieval-Augmented Generation framework, enhancing the data processing capabilities in AI applications.\n- My work in Agentic AI primarily revolves around building AI solutions that respond dynamically to user queries, which I have implemented in my current role at Deloitte.\n- I reside in Gurugram, which provides easy access to project locations in the NCR region.\n\nI look forward to discussing my application in more detail. Thank you for your time, and please let me know if there are any further questions.\n\nBest regards,\nManu Yadav\n\nContact: +91-7791997383\nEmail: peyadavmanu57@gmail.com\nLinkedIn: /in/manuyadav"},{"id":"19e894a5acb0edb6","subject":"Fwd: Job Opportunity at Barclays | BA4 - Data Scientist","body":"Hi. Manu ,\r\n\r\n\r\nWe were unable to reach you on your mobile.\r\n\r\nWe wanted to discuss an exciting opportunity for the role of BA4 - Data\r\nScientist at Barclays. Please find the job details below for your\r\nreference. If you are keen to pursue this ahead, *share your updated\r\nresume* with\r\nus at the earliest. Also, share the below details:\r\n\r\n   - Current CTC:\r\n   - .Expected CTC:\r\n   - Notice Period:\r\n   - Reason For Change:\r\n\r\nCould you also share the answers to the following?:\r\n\r\n\r\n   - *Question: Do you have hands on exp in Pyspark ?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n   - *Question: Do you have exp in unstructured data ?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n   - *Question: How many years of Data Science or Data Analytics exp you\r\n   have ?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n*Company Profile Link:*\r\nhttps://careerpage.hirebound.io/td_newton/barclays/position/M6YR8E\r\n\r\n*About The Company:*\r\n\r\nBarclays is a British universal bank. Our vision is to be the UK-centred\r\nleader in global finance. We are a diversified bank with comprehensive UK\r\nconsumer, corporate and wealth and private banking franchises, a leading\r\ninvestment bank and a strong, specialist US consumer bank. Through these\r\nfive divisions, we are working togethe.r for a better financial future for\r\nour customers, clients and communities. With over 325 years of history and\r\nexpertise in banking, Barclays operates in over 40 countries and employs\r\napproximately 83,500 people. Barclays moves, lends, invests and protects\r\nmoney for customers and clients worldwide. Barclays is a trading name of\r\nBarclays Bank PLC and its subsidiaries. Barclays Bank PLC is registered in\r\nEngland and is authorised by the Prudential Regulation Authority and\r\nregulated by the Financial Conduct Authority and the Prudential Regulation\r\nAuthority. Registered in England. Registered No. 1026167. Registered\r\noffice: 1 Churchill Place, London E14 5HP.\r\n\r\n*Job Description*\r\n\r\n*Purpose of the role*\r\n\r\nTo use innovative data analytics and machine learning techniques to extract\r\nvaluable insights from the bank's data reserves, leveraging these insights\r\nto inform strategic decision-making, improve operational efficiency, and\r\ndrive innovation across the organisation.\r\n\r\n*Accountabilities*\r\n\r\n   - Identification, collection, extraction of data from various sources,\r\n   including internal and external sources.\r\n   - Performing data cleaning, wrangling, and transformation to ensure its\r\n   quality and suitability for analysis.\r\n   - Development and maintenance of efficient data pipelines for automated\r\n   data acquisition and processing.\r\n   - Design and conduct of statistical and machine learning models to\r\n   analyse patterns, trends, and relationships in the data.\r\n   - Development and implementation of predictive models to forecast future\r\n   outcomes and identify potential risks and opportunities.\r\n   - Collaborate with business stakeholders to seek out opportunities to\r\n   add value from data through Data Science.\r\n\r\n*Analyst Expectations*\r\n\r\n\r\n   - T.o perform prescribed activities in a timely manner and to a high\r\n   standard consistently driving continuous improvement.\r\n   - Requires in-depth technical knowledge and experience in their assigned\r\n   area of expertise\r\n   - Thorough understanding of the underlying principles and concepts\r\n   within the area of expertise\r\n   - They lead and supervise a team, guiding and supporting professional\r\n   development, allocating work requirements and coordinating team resources.\r\n   - If the position has leadership responsibilities, People Leaders are\r\n   expected to demonstrate a clear set of leadership behaviours to create an\r\n   environment for colleagues to thrive and deliver to a consistently\r\n   excellent standard. The four LEAD behaviours are: L – Listen and be\r\n   authentic, E – Energise and inspire, A – Align across the enterprise, D –\r\n   Develop others.\r\n   - OR for an individual contributor, they develop technical expertise in\r\n   work area, acting as an advisor where appropriate.\r\n   - Will have an impact on the work of related teams within the area.\r\n   - Partner with other functions and business areas.\r\n   - Takes responsibility for end results of a team’s operational\r\n   processing and activities.\r\n   - Escalate breaches of policies / procedure appropriately.\r\n   - Take responsibility for embedding new policies/ procedures adopted due\r\n   to risk mitigation.\r\n   - Advise and influence decision making within own area of expertise.\r\n   - Take ownership for managing risk and strengthening controls in\r\n   relation to the work you own or contribute to. Deliver your work and areas\r\n   of responsibility in line with relevant rules, regulation and codes of\r\n   conduct.\r\n   - Maintain and continually build an understanding of how own\r\n   sub-function integrates with function, alongside knowledge of the\r\n   organisations products, services and processes within the function.\r\n   - Demonstrate understanding of how areas coordinate and contribute to\r\n   the achievement of the objectives of the organisation sub-function.\r\n   - Make evaluative judgements based on the analysis of factual\r\n   information, paying attention to detail.\r\n   - Resolve problems by identifying and selecting solutions through the\r\n   application of acquired technical experience and will be guided by\r\n   precedents.\r\n   - Guide and persuade team members and communicate complex / sensitive\r\n   information.\r\n   - Act as contact point for stakeholders outside of the immediate\r\n   function, while building a network of contacts outside team and external to\r\n   the organisation.\r\n\r\nAll colleagues will be expected to demonstrate the Barclays Values of\r\nRespect, Integrity, Service, Excellence and Stewardship – our moral\r\ncompass, helping us do what we believe is right. They will also be expected\r\nto demonstrate the Barclays Mindset – to Empower, Challenge and Drive – the\r\noperating manual for how we behave.\r\n\r\nJoin us as a “Data Scientist”, within the Controls Analytics and Insight\r\nteam, supporting the Chief Controls Office function.\r\n\r\nYou may be assessed on key critical skills relevant for success in role,\r\nsuch as risk and controls, change and transformation, business acumen,\r\nstrategic thinking and digital and technology, as well as job-specific\r\ntechnical skills.\r\n\r\nTo be successful as a “Data Scientist”, you should have experience with:\r\n\r\n\r\n*Basic/ Essential Qualifications:*\r\n\r\n   - Experience performing quantitative analysis given a defined scope and\r\n   translating results into meaningful business insights. A.bility to adapt\r\n   and appreciate changing business contexts.\r\n   - Ability to identify and learn emerging DS and AI tools and\r\n   technologies and utilise them to deliver practical business solutions; be a\r\n   self explorer.\r\n   - Experience on Python, SQL, and strong ability to work with large and\r\n   complex data.\r\n   - Knowledge of best practices in data storage, retrieval, and\r\n   manipulation and data visualization techniques.\r\n\r\n*Basic/ Essential Qualifications:*\r\n\r\n   - Recognised degree/ certification in STEM discipline.\r\n   - Strong verbal and written communication skills, and ability to\r\n   interface with Business and CCO teams.\r\n\r\nThis role will be based out of Gurugram.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nMegha Gupta | 7042199329\r\n\r\nTD Newton & Associates"},{"id":"19e89464b2df527b","subject":"Fwd: Job Opportunity at KPMG |  Con\\AM - Generative AI Engineer","body":"Hi Manu ,\r\n\r\n.\r\nThank you for your confirming your interest for the role of Con\\AM -\r\nGenerative AI Engineer at KPMG . Please find the job details below for your\r\nreference. If you are keen to pursue this ahead, *share your updated\r\nresume* with\r\nus at the earliest. Also, share the below details:\r\n\r\n   - Current CTC:\r\n   - Expected CTC:\r\n   - Notice Period:\r\n   - Reason For Job Change:\r\n\r\n\r\n   - *Question: Do you have experience developing AI models using\r\n   TensorFlow, PyTorch, or Keras?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n   - *Question: Can you describe a project where you implemented advanced\r\n   AI techniques such as Generative AI or Reinforcement Learning?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n   - *Question: Do you have experience deploying AI models in cloud\r\n   environments, particularly Azure?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n   - *Question: do you have exp in RAG framework ?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n   - *Question: What kind of work have you done in Agentic AI ?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:\r\n   - *Question: where do you stay in Delhi\\NCR ?*\r\n\r\n   Answer:.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n*Company Profile Link*:\r\nhttps://careerpage.hirebound.io/td_newton/kpmg/position/01990e82-79c1-7221-9df6-de1ff6af9f2f\r\n\r\n\r\n*About The Company: *\r\n\r\nKPMG is a global network of professional firms providing Audit, Tax and\r\nAdvisory services. We have 227,000 outstanding professionals working\r\ntogether to deliver value in 146 countries and territories. With a\r\nworldwide presence, KPMG continues to build on our successes thanks to\r\nclear vision, defined values and, above all, our people. Our industry focus\r\nhelps KPMG firms’ professionals develop a rich understanding of clients'\r\nbusinesses and the insight, skills and resources required to address\r\nindustry-specific issues and opportunities. The independent member firms of\r\nthe KPMG network are affiliated with KPMG International Cooperative (“KPMG\r\nInternational”), a Swiss entity. Each KPMG firm is a legally distinct and\r\nseparate entity and describes itself as such.\r\n\r\n• *Proposed designation : Consultant\\ Assistant Manager*\r\n• *Role type:* Individual contributor\r\n• *Reporting to:* Manager\r\n• *Geo to be supported:* KPMG Delivery Network (KDN)\r\n\r\nKPMG Delivery Network (KDN) is seeking a highly skilled AI Engineer to join\r\nour pioneering team. This role is crucial for developing and deploying\r\nadvanced *AI solutions, leveraging cutting-edge technologies such as\r\nGenerative AI, Machine Learning, Deep Learning, Neural Networks, and\r\nReinforcement Learning. *The AI Engineer will be responsible for designing,\r\ncoding, and implementing AI components, services, and libraries, working\r\nclosely with a development team to bring AI products from concept to\r\nmarket.\r\n\r\nAs an AI Engineer, you will lead the technical execution of *AI projects,\r\nfrom initial prototyping to production and market launch, ensuring that AI\r\nsolutions are built to the highest standards of performance, scalability,\r\nand security. *\r\n\r\nKey responsibilities include:\r\n1. AI Solution Development:\r\n• *Work on design and development of AI models and algorithms using\r\nframeworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, and Keras. *\r\n*•* *Develop and cod/e robust AI components, services, and libraries,\r\nensuring they are scalable, maintainable, and optimized for performance. *\r\n*•* *Implement advanced AI techniques, including Generative AI,\r\nReinforcement Learning, and Fine-Tuning, to solve complex business\r\nproblems. *\r\n2. Technical Leadership and Collaboration:\r\n• Collaborate with AI architects, data scientists, and software engineers\r\nto design and build end-to-end AI solutions.\r\n• Provide technical leadership to the development team, guiding them\r\nthrough the design, coding, testing, and deployment of AI models.\r\n• Engage with KPMG member firms and other stakeholders to understand their\r\nrequirements and translate them into technical solutions.\r\n\r\n3. AI Product Lifecycle Management:\r\n• Work on all phases of the AI product lifecycle, including prototype\r\ndevelopment, proof of concept (PoC), minimum viable product (MVP), and\r\nfull-scale production.\r\n• Work closely with product management and testing teams to ensure that AI\r\nproducts are developed/ launched according to specifications and timelines.\r\n• Drive the continuous improvement of AI products, incorporating user\r\nfeedback and new technological advancements.\r\n\r\n4. Cloud and Infrastructure Management:\r\n• *Deploy AI models and services in cloud environments, primarily using\r\nAzure, ensuring scalability, reliability, and security. *\r\n*•* *Implement CI/CD pipelines, Docker containers, and Kubernetes for\r\nefficient AI model deployment and management. *\r\n• Optimize the infrastructure for AI workloads, ensuring cost-effectiveness\r\nand high performance.\r\n5. Research & Innovation:\r\n• Stay up-to-date with the latest developments in AI and machine learning,\r\nexperimenting with new tools, frameworks, and methodologies.\r\n• Innovate and propose new AI-driven use cases that can bring value to KDN\r\nand its member firms.\r\n• Contribute to the development of AI best practices, coding standards, and\r\ntechnical documentation.\r\n6. Security & Compliance:\r\n• Ensure that all AI solutions comply with KDN’s data privacy, security,\r\nand regulatory requirements.\r\n• Implement security best practices in AI model development and deployment,\r\nsafeguarding sensitive data and intellectual property.\r\n\r\n*Educational qualifications*\r\n• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data\r\nScience, or a related field.\r\n• Advanced certifications in AI/ML, cloud computing, or software\r\nengineering are advantageous.\r\n\r\n*Work experience*\r\n• experience in AI, Machine Learning, or related fields, with hands-on\r\nexperience in developing and deploying AI solutions.\r\n*•* *Proven experience with AI frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, and\r\nKeras, and cloud platforms like Azure. *\r\n• Strong background in softw.are development, including experience with\r\nPython.\r\n• Experience leading AI projects through all phases, from prototype to\r\nproduction.\r\n\r\n*Skills*\r\n• Expertise in designing and coding AI components, services, and libraries.\r\n*•* *Strong understanding of AI/ML algorithms, model optimization, and\r\ndeployment strategies. *\r\n• Proficiency in cloud-based AI development and deployment, particularly\r\nwith Azure.\r\n*•* *Familiarity with DevOps practices, including CI/CD pipelines, Docker,\r\nand Kubernetes. *\r\n• Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to work collaboratively\r\nin a cross-functional team environment.\r\n• Strong communication skills, with the ability to translate complex\r\ntechnical concepts into actionable solutions.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks and Regards\r\n\r\nRiya Bisht | Associate Consultant\r\n\r\nEmail: riya.bisht@tdnewton.com\r\n\r\nPhone No.: 9910971740\r\n\r\n<http://www.tdnewton.com/>\r\n\r\nSuite No 3B , AIHP Business Centre, AIHP Palms , Plot No.242,243\r\n\r\nUdyog Vihar - Phase 4 , Gurugram 122015"}]}
